{"step_index":620,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T17:59:20Z","content":"**Updated to `gemini-3.6-flash` and deployed live to Surge!**\n\n---\n\n### What Was Updated:\n1. **Model Upgraded:** Both the **Vision AI Lead Sheet Parser** and the **AI SMS Copywriting Engine** are now updated to **`gemini-3.6-flash`**.\n2. **Resilient Multi-Model Fallbacks:** Added automatic tier fallbacks (`gemini-3.6-flash` $\\rightarrow$ `gemini-2.0-flash` $\\rightarrow$ `gemini-1.5-flash`) so the app adapts seamlessly across different Google AI Studio key tiers.\n3. **Compiled & Deployed Live:** Rebuilt and published directly to **[https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh](https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh)**.\n\n---\n\n### Test on Your Phone:\nSimply open **SnapDialer** on your iPhone (or refresh the page), snap your lead sheet, and it will process directly with Gemini 3.6 Flash!"}
{"step_index":621,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T18:03:46Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nthe app seems to be making individual lists for each lead added.  this would be okay if i were grabbing multiple leads from one sheet, but each photo i import represents only one lead...not multiple.  i think we need to abandon the whole 'list' philosophy and just recognize that we're working with a bunch of individual leads.  we can capture the date/time the entered the system, but maintaining entire separate lists with dates is not necessary\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-20T14:03:46-04:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":622,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T18:03:47Z","thinking":"**Defining the Core Workflow**\n\nOkay, I've got a handle on the user's workflow. It appears each imported photo represents a single FRS Report Card from ValuTeachers. That's a key piece of the puzzle and now I can start evaluating the impacts.\n\n\n**Reimagining the App Architecture**\n\nI'm now focusing on restructuring the app's core architecture. The redesign centers around a unified \"Educator Lead Hub,\" replacing the cumbersome list-based system. The home screen will become an Educator Lead Pipeline, displaying all leads in a single view with filtering and sorting capabilities. A dynamic top bar will give key stats at a glance.\n\n\n**Implementing New Functionality**\n\nI'm now integrating crucial features. There's a powerful search function by name, school, or room number, and date/time capture for added context. The power dialer queue is a priority, offering one-tap dialing and filtering by lead status. Streamlined \"Snap Sheet\" workflow saves leads with a single tap, bypassing list management. Direct lead actions are also being implemented for each card.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\brorm\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\snap-dialer\\\\src\\\\db\\\\leadsRepository.ts\"","toolAction":"\"Viewing leadsRepository.ts\"","toolSummary":"\"View leadsRepository.ts\""}}]}
{"step_index":623,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T18:03:52Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-20T14:03:52-04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-20T14:03:52-04:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/db/leadsRepository.ts`\nTotal Lines: 215\nTotal Bytes: 7278\nShowing lines 1 to 215\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: import { getDatabase } from './database';\n2: import { Lead, LeadList, CallDisposition, ExtractedLeadItem } from '../types';\n3: \n4: export class LeadsRepository {\n5:   static async createListWithLeads(\n6:     title: string,\n7:     imageUri: string | null,\n8:     leads: ExtractedLeadItem[]\n9:   ): Promise<LeadList> {\n10:     const db = await getDatabase();\n11:     const listId = 'list_' + Date.now() + '_' + Math.random().toString(36).substring(2, 7);\n12:     const now = new Date().toISOString();\n13: \n14:     const validLeads = leads.filter((l) => l.name.trim() && l.phone.trim());\n15: \n16:     await db.withTransactionAsync(async () => {\n17:       await db.runAsync(\n18:         `INSERT INTO lists (id, title, source_image_uri, total_leads, completed_leads, connected_leads, created_at, updated_at)\n19:          VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, 0, 0, ?, ?)`,\n20:         [listId, title, imageUri, validLeads.length, now, now]\n21:       );\n22: \n23:       for (const item of validLeads) {\n24:         const leadId = 'lead_' + Date.now() + '_' + Math.random().toString(36).substring(2, 7);\n25:         await db.runAsync(\n26:           `INSERT INTO leads (\n27:             id, list_id, name, phone, school, email, age, planning_period, \n28:             room_number, years_in_frs, text_ok, frs_knowledge, frs_interests, \n29:             custom_questions, meeting_preferences, annual_salary, present_403b_contribution, \n30:             source_image_uri, company, notes, cadence_step, last_disposition, attempts_count, created_at, updated_at\n31:           ) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, \n<truncated 4712 bytes>\nd_at = ? \n156:            WHERE id = ?`,\n157:           [stats.completed || 0, stats.connected || 0, now, lead.list_id]\n158:         );\n159:       }\n160:     });\n161:   }\n162: \n163:   static async scheduleFollowUp(leadId: string, followUpDateISO: string, note?: string): Promise<void> {\n164:     const db = await getDatabase();\n165:     const now = new Date().toISOString();\n166:     await db.runAsync(\n167:       `UPDATE leads \n168:        SET follow_up_at = ?, \n169:            last_disposition = 'callback_requested', \n170:            notes = COALESCE(?, notes), \n171:            updated_at = ? \n172:        WHERE id = ?`,\n173:       [followUpDateISO, note || null, now, leadId]\n174:     );\n175:   }\n176: \n177:   static async getUpcomingFollowUps(): Promise<Lead[]> {\n178:     const db = await getDatabase();\n179:     const rawLeads = await db.getAllAsync<any>(\n180:       `SELECT * FROM leads \n181:        WHERE follow_up_at IS NOT NULL \n182:        ORDER BY follow_up_at ASC`\n183:     );\n184:     return rawLeads.map(this.hydrateLead);\n185:   }\n186: \n187:   private static hydrateLead(raw: any): Lead {\n188:     let interests: string[] = [];\n189:     let preferences: string[] = [];\n190: \n191:     if (typeof raw.frs_interests === 'string') {\n192:       try {\n193:         interests = JSON.parse(raw.frs_interests);\n194:       } catch {}\n195:     } else if (Array.isArray(raw.frs_interests)) {\n196:       interests = raw.frs_interests;\n197:     }\n198: \n199:     if (typeof raw.meeting_preferences === 'string') {\n200:       try {\n201:         preferences = JSON.parse(raw.meeting_preferences);\n202:       } catch {}\n203:     } else if (Array.isArray(raw.meeting_preferences)) {\n204:       preferences = raw.meeting_preferences;\n205:     }\n206: \n207:     return {\n208:       ...raw,\n209:       text_ok: raw.text_ok === 1 || raw.text_ok === true,\n210:       frs_interests: interests,\n211:       meeting_preferences: preferences,\n212:     };\n213:   }\n214: }\n215: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
